  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added an ordinary CPython-parseable semantic layer for leading and constant coefficients, valuation, parent-aware monic construction, domain-owned content, squarefreeness, squarefree decompositions, radicals, and exact default-parent roots. Production valuation is explicitly one storage-aware callback while the coefficient scan remains a portable oracle. Squarefreeness and radical construction use scalar-content and primitive squarefree-part callbacks rather than full irreducible factorization. Already-monic inputs preserve identity without allocation, and root collection combines equal values across mixed hashable and unhashable exact representations. Sage.js and CPython tests pin the chosen ZZ/QQ zero semantics, signed scalar normalization, parent widening, multiplicities, and default root domains.",
    "risks": [
      "This is an unwired contract module; public PolynomialElement integration must supply generated resource operations and must not turn the callbacks into coefficient-by-coefficient host crossings.",
      "The contract deliberately defines zero as not squarefree in both exact domains, following the mathematical contract and task requirement even though SageMath 10.9's QQ implementation currently reports True.",
      "ZZ squarefreeness and radicals require mature scalar-content and primitive-part callbacks; generated resource integration must keep these as bulk operations rather than coefficient-by-coefficient crossings.",
      "The public resource layer still has to supply the one-boundary valuation callback and direct squarefree-part primitives; this lane defines and differentially tests their storage-neutral semantic contract."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Add invariants.py to the strict Pyright and node test manifests in the integration lane.",
      "Wire the public ZZ and QQ polynomial methods to these contracts using generated FLINT resource callbacks for valuation, content, primitive squarefree tests/parts, squarefree decomposition, factorization, and result construction.",
      "Retain the CPython and dynamic witnesses as differential oracles when native public wiring is added."
    ]
  }
}
